    "text": "advice 1  \nTalk to someone you trust. It's okay to feel confused or unsure about who you are. Sharing your feelings with a friend, family member, or counselor can help you feel less alone and gain new perspectives.\n\n***\nadvice 2  \nBe kind to yourself. Identity is a journey, and it's okay to have moments of self-doubt. Celebrate small victories and focus on progress rather than perfection.\n\n***\nadvice 3  \nExplore your interests and values. Try new activities, read books, or engage in hobbies that make you feel seen and valued. This can help you discover who you are and what you stand for.",
